-  code %/main

=  recall
  '  when next (an epoch nat, supplied with the grade), gap width
  '  (days), ease (x1000)
  !  srs/due n
  !  srs/interval n
  !  srs/ease n

=  card recall
  '  a card is recall metadata plus the prompt: front/back text of
  '  its own, or about pointing at any namespace node whose content
  '  is the prompt
  !  front t | about path
  ?  back t

=  deck
  !  title t

#  finish_card
  '  mark a card with its review feedback: grade (0 again, 1 hard,
  '  2 good, 3 easy) and when (the review time, an epoch nat) poke
  '  together; the review behavior computes the next schedule in the
  '  same event and consumes the grade
  :  recall
  >
    :  srs/grade  n
    :  srs/when  n
  <
    recall

+  srs "spaced repetition: cards, decks, and the review clock"
  +  cards
    *  ts card
    +  what_is_a_shrine_name card
      "the starter card"
      :  front "What does a Shrine name identify?"
      :  back "A versioned locus of state."
      :  srs/due 0
      :  srs/interval 0
      :  srs/ease 2500
  +  decks
    *  ts deck
  +  next
    "the review queue: a spun view over the cards, limit at a time"
    :  weft code#next
    :  limit 10
    :  tack '?/y;%/srs/cards
